00:04:10,909 --> 00:04:16,909
Every war has a beginning.

2
00:08:21,818 --> 00:08:27,818
Underworld: Rise of the Lycans is a fantasy, action,
thriller film directed by Patrick Tatopoulos.

3
00:12:32,727 --> 00:12:38,727
A prequel to the first two Underworld films, this fantasy explains the
origins of the feud between the Vampires and the Lycans.

4
00:16:43,636 --> 00:16:49,636
Aided by his secret love, Sonja, courageous Lucian leads the
Lycans in battle against brutal Vampire king Viktor.

5
00:20:54,545 --> 00:21:00,545
Determined to break the king's enslavement of his people, Lucian faces off
against the Death Dealer army in a bid for Lycan independence.

6
00:25:05,454 --> 00:25:11,454
Sonja, played by Rhona Mitra.

7
00:29:16,363 --> 00:29:22,363
Viktor, played by Bill Nighy.

8
00:33:27,272 --> 00:33:33,272
Lucian, played by Michael Sheen.

9
00:37:38,181 --> 00:37:44,181
Kraven, played by Shane Brolly.

10
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:55,090
Andreas Tanis, played by Steven Mackintosh.

11
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Raze, played by Kevin Grevioux.

12
00:50:10,909 --> 00:50:16,909
Underworld: Rise of the Lycans is a 2009 American action horror film directed by Patrick Tatopoulos from a screenplay by
Danny McBride, Dirk Blackman, Howard McCain, based on a story by Len Wiseman, Robert Orr, and McBride.

13
00:54:21,818 --> 00:54:27,818
It is a prequel to Underworld (2003) and the third
installment in the Underworld film series.

14
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
The film stars Michael Sheen, Bill Nighy, Rhona Mitra,
Steven Mackintosh, and Kevin Grevioux.

15
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
The plot focuses primarily on the origins of the characters and
the events that lead up to the Vampire–Lycan war.

16
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
Kate Beckinsale, who starred in the previous Underworld
films, appears briefly at the end of the film.

17
01:11:05,454 --> 01:11:11,454
Underworld: Rise of the Lycans premiered at the ArcLight Hollywood in Los Angeles, California on January
22, 2009, and was released in the United States on January 23, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

18
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
The film received generally negative reviews from critics and grossed over
$91 million against its production budget of $35 million.

19
01:19:27,272 --> 01:19:33,272
The film was followed by Underworld: Awakening, in 2012, serving as
a direct sequel to Underworld: Evolution (2006).

20
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
The film explores themes of prison, vampire, slavery, castle, forbidden love.

21
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The tone is dark and intense.
